From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:19:55 +0200
Subject: [parser] Fix over-marking variables as assigned in ValidatePattern

When validating a destructuring assignment pattern,
ExpressionParsingScope::ValidatePattern previously iterated over the
entire variable_list_ from index 0, marking variables from earlier
subexpressions in the same ExpressionParsingScope (such as comma
operands, call arguments, or array/object elements) as assigned.
Additionally, property assignment targets inside destructuring patterns
(e.g. '[obj.prop, a] = [1, 2]') left their receiver and key variables in
variable_list_, causing ValidatePattern to mark them as assigned too.

Track the starting index in variable_list_ before parsing an assignment
LHS or destructuring sub-pattern, discard variables from property
targets once validated as expressions, and only mark variables starting
from the pattern's lhs_variable_index as assigned. Also restrict
ExpressionScope::SetInitializers to CanBeArrowParameterDeclaration()
scopes.

